{"type":"standard","title":"Ned Lamont","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ned Lamont</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q1973878","titles":{"canonical":"Ned_Lamont","normalized":"Ned Lamont","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ned Lamont</span></span>"},"pageid":3651812,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Governor_Ned_Lamont_of_Connecticut%2C_official_portrait.jpg/330px-Governor_Ned_Lamont_of_Connecticut%2C_official_portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":452},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b8/Governor_Ned_Lamont_of_Connecticut%2C_official_portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1453,"height":1990},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375080236","tid":"94a096b3-b139-11f1-bb5f-bce5c5022580","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:13:49Z","description":"Governor of Connecticut since 2019","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ned_Lamont","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ned_Lamont?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ned_Lamont?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ned_Lamont"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ned_Lamont","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ned_Lamont","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ned_Lamont?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ned_Lamont"}},"extract":"Edward Miner Lamont Jr. is an American politician and businessman serving since 2019 as the 89th governor of Connecticut. A member of the Democratic Party, he served from 1987 to 1989 as a Greenwich selectman, and was the Democratic nominee for the United States Senate in 2006, losing to Independent incumbent Joe Lieberman.","extract_html":"<p><b>Edward Miner Lamont Jr.</b> is an American politician and businessman serving since 2019 as the 89th governor of Connecticut. A member of the Democratic Party, he served from 1987 to 1989 as a Greenwich selectman, and was the Democratic nominee for the United States Senate in 2006, losing to Independent incumbent Joe Lieberman.</p>"}